  "evidence_class": "MEASURED_ON_MARVEL_NOT_YET_VALIDATED_ON_AVP",
  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "The VDP2 register block reads back as all zeros, so layer enables, plane maps, priorities and scroll values cannot be decoded from this capture.",
      "consequence": "VDP2 layer responsibility stays UNRESOLVED for an instrument reason, not for lack of analysis. Resolving it needs a different instrument, not a better parser.",
      "evidence": "MEASURED",
      "falsification": "A capture in which any VDP2 register byte is non-zero, which would show the register block is in fact readable.",
      "holds": true,
      "id": "VDP2-1"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Every VDP1 sprite colour bank measured at every anchor resolves into a populated 16-colour bank of VDP2 colour RAM.",
      "consequence": "VDP2 owns sprite colour for the VDP1 actor path. Colour-bank mode sprites cost colour-RAM banks, which is a VDP2 budget, not a VDP1 texture budget.",
      "evidence": "MEASURED",
      "falsification": "A referenced CMDCOLR bank whose colour-RAM bank is entirely zero, which would mean the bank index is being read wrongly.",
      "holds": true,
      "id": "VDP2-2"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Only a small fixed set of SCSP slots holds any register content, and their registers are byte-identical across the whole window.",
      "consequence": "Attack and impact audio are not delivered by keying a fresh SCSP slot per game event in this window.",
      "evidence": "MEASURED",
      "falsification": "An anchor at which a previously-zero slot becomes non-zero, or at which any active slot's registers differ from another anchor's.",
      "holds": true,
      "id": "SCSP-1"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sound RAM changes on every transition while the slot registers do not, which fits a continuously-playing buffer that a sound program refills rather than per-event slot key-on.",
      "consequence": "The audio adapter should model a mixed stream plus a small static slot set, and treat per-event routing as a sound-program concern.",
      "evidence": "INFERRED",
      "falsification": "A trace showing slot key-on writes between the captured anchors, which a four-frame sample would miss; or an anchor whose sound RAM is unchanged while audio is audibly playing.",
      "holds": true,
      "id": "SCSP-2"
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Four sampled frames cannot show a register write that happens between them; only a write trace can.",
    "A static slot register set does not prove which sample is playing or which cue it represents.",
    "Colour-bank resolution assumes CMDCOLR's low bits are a colour-RAM entry index in colour-bank mode; the join succeeding is consistent with that, not a proof of the bit width.",
    "VDP2 VRAM stability during combat says nothing about load-time layer ownership.",
    "No count, slot index, bank index or page total here is a budget for any other title."
  ],
  "method": "Compare the VDP2 register block, colour RAM, VDP2 VRAM, SCSP register block and sound RAM at the four normal-hit anchors, and resolve every measured VDP1 CMDCOLR bank into a colour-RAM bank.",
  "purpose": "Close the VDP2 and audio gaps left by the VDP1 command analysis",
  "title": "MSHvSF Saturn VDP2 colour ownership and SCSP slot activity",
